🤖 DeepEP internode update: the JAX autodiff plumbing is now complete in this worktree for normal-mode internode transport.

What changed:
- added `levanter_deepep_dispatch_internode_cached` as a C++/FFI target;
- added `_dispatch_internode_cached_impl` in the JAX wrapper;
- wrapped `deepep_combine_internode` in a custom VJP so combine backward routes `grad_combined_x` through cached internode dispatch;
- threaded `recv_gbl_rank_prefix_sum` through the combine API, Grug `deepep_internode` backend, remat checkpoint names, and the CW runtime smoke;
- added a static autodiff contract test proving combine backward calls `levanter_deepep_dispatch_internode_cached`.

Validation run:
- `uv run python -m py_compile lib/levanter/src/levanter/kernels/deepep/transport_ffi.py lib/levanter/src/levanter/grug/_moe/ep_deepep.py experiments/grug/moe/launch_cw_deepep_runtime_smoke.py`
- `uv run pytest lib/levanter/tests/kernels/test_deepep_availability.py -q -k 'internode and (dispatch or combine)'` -> 4 passed
- `uv run pytest lib/levanter/tests/grug/test_grugformer_moe.py -q -k 'deepep_internode or tokens_per_rdma_rank'` -> 3 passed
- targeted `./infra/pre-commit.py ...` over the touched DeepEP/Grug/doc files -> OK

Remaining before calling it train-step-ready: rebuild/load the updated transport on CW, run the process-per-GPU DeepEP dispatch+combine smoke, then run a tiny Grug train-step smoke with `moe_implementation=deepep_internode` (EP16 is a good first comparison target). Debug log updated in `docs/debug-log-deepep-internode-jax.md`.
